From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 00:57:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: stub HTTP/proxy modules, rustls ring provider

- net/http_wasm.rs: on wasm32 the net::http module (selected via
  #[cfg]+#[path]) is a thin adapter that maps core's HTTP API onto
  tokio-wasm-shim's tokio::net::fetch; the fetch()/web-sys plumbing lives
  in crates/tokio-wasm-shim. The browser owns TLS/redirects/caching;
  requests are subject to CORS (apps.testrun.org sends ACAO:*, so the
  webxdc apps list works). The read_url*/post_* wrappers use a 60s timeout
  (browser fetch() has none). The adapter lands with the wiring because
  upstream's net/http.rs needs hyper, which wasm32 doesn't build; a stack
  cut off before the adapter would compile that file and fail.
- net/proxy_wasm.rs: compile-compatible stub selected via #[cfg]+#[path];
  proxies need raw TCP, so every operation errors at runtime.
- tls: default_provider() helper -> aws-lc-rs native, ring on wasm;
  non-strict TLS falls back to rustls (no native-tls on wasm)
- session: gate native-tls/socks5/shadowsocks SessionStream impls
- qr: shadowsocks QR decoding errors on wasm
---
